eds and the americas  and other weeds to other parts of the  country  i found that enlightening so this was an  introduced and naturalized  weed the seeds however of this one  contain lysergic acid amide  not the diethyl form anyway interesting  side  branch there we have  in vietnam excuse me one second  there are so many different types of  rubus i was  overwhelmed rumi's sumatranus  is a raspberry type the fruit  dehiscence from the taurus and it forms  sort of a globe  unless it collapses uh and  it can be distinguished by the red hairs  besides the nodal prickles that it has  on the stem  and for each of these trips we prepare  voucher specimens  besides collecting wild materials  and for voucher specimens we have  presses  and not only do we collect terrestrial  plants  but sometimes we need a mountain elf to  climb up  an oak tree to reach the epiphytic type  plants that are above  our heads and so jim oliphant was our  mountain elf  an expert tree climber to obtain  some of these high located germplasm  vaccinium relatives  another type of rubus rubus reflexus  uh we had four different varieties  botanical varieties that were present in  vietnam where we were and i'll just  show you a close-up of one of the  stipules  uh it's a way that rubus uh can be  uh separated from other species  fancy pan as i mentioned is the highest  in indochina  and it's uh was a long climb  uh there's a hut um actually  about a third of the way up there's a  second hut  another third of the way up before you  hike up  to the very top and around  the halfway point at this hut where we  spent the night  there are many rubus species  this particular one is rubis  glabrocarpus  and this hawaii was just taking a photo  of this very interesting tri-lobal  rubus species jim  and ken and also several  of our sherpas we did have sherpas going  up this mountain who  carried our food for us  they hiked up the whole summit  to 3000 meters and a group of us stayed  back  and collected rubus f